  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nClique Bait is an innovative online seafood store founded by Danny, a former member of a digital data analytics team. The store aims to leverage data analytics insights to enhance its operations and user experience. This project involves analyzing event data to understand and improve the customer journey on Clique Bait's website.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to calculate funnel fallout rates for the Clique Bait online store. This involves combining and analyzing multiple datasets to uncover insights that can help optimize the customer journey and reduce drop-offs.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Founder & CEO: Danny, who wants to integrate data analytics into the seafood industry.\n- Customers: Visitors to the Clique Bait website, identified through their `cookie_id`.\n- Data Analysts: Individuals who will analyze the data to derive insights and support decision-making.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Collection: Collect data from various datasets, including user visits, events, campaigns, and page hierarchy.\n- Data Integration: Combine the five datasets using keys such as `cookie_id`, `event_type`, and `page_id`.\n- Event Tracking: Utilize `event_type` and `page_id` to track customer interactions on the website, leveraging the `event_identifier` and `page_hierarchy` tables.\n- Campaign Analysis: Analyze campaign data from `campaign_identifier` to assess the impact on customer behavior.\n- Funnel Analysis: Calculate funnel fallout rates using the sequenced events to identify where customers drop off in the purchase process.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: The system should efficiently handle large datasets and provide timely insights.\n- Scalability: The analytical processes should scale to accommodate more data as the company grows.\n- Accuracy: Ensure precise linking of data across datasets for accurate analysis and insights.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0198\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `cookie_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cookie_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `events` (\n  `visit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cookie_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `event_type` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `page_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `event_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`visit_id`,`event_type`),\n  KEY `events_ibfk_1` (`cookie_id`),\n  KEY `events_ibfk_2` (`event_type`),\n  KEY `events_ibfk_3` (`page_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `events_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cookie_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`cookie_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `events_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`event_type`) REFERENCES `event_identifier` (`event_type`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `events_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `page_hierarchy` (`page_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `event_identifier` (\n  `event_type` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `event_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`event_type`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `campaign_identifier` (\n  `campaign_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `campaign_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`campaign_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `page_hierarchy` (\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `page_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`page_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
